This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Silver golems: Just like gold golems, except it's silver. When
killed, it crumbles into various types of silver equipment. Undead
avoid them like the plague... or whatever the equivilant of the plague
is to undead. --TheShrewdDude_

[2]: The Bank of Yendor: It's where you go to deposit your cash. And to
withdraw checks and bank notes and whatnot. It's not exactly like Fort
Ludios, because the Bank is guarded by shopkeepers. Or bankkeepers.
--TheShrewdDude_

[3]: Swimming skill: Who doesn't want to have a quick refreshing dip
once in a while? At unskilled, you'll have to skinny-dip to avoid
drowning, but by basic you can manage to take some weight with you,
though it might be soaked. At skilled or above, you can bathe with your
items with impunity, and by Grand Master you'll have access to all
sorts of aquatic fun with foocubi. --TheShrewdDude_

[4]: when #offering, your god should sometimes grant a wish or a
(blessed?) genocide in place of an artifact --teabing_

[5]: Zapless condcut. No wands. --SomeoneElseYes

[6]: Archaeologists should have some sort of bonues against rolling
boulder traps (Indiana Jones) --ilya86

[7]: kicking a wall should be insta-death by falling boulders and rocks
--shambler

[8]: Items should retain their appearance when identified. (ie. i - a
shiny ring of free action; Q - a mottled spellbook of stone to flesh)
--TheShrewdDude

[9]: In real life, it's dangerous to use a tinning kit if you don't
know what you're doing. This should apply to Nethack as well. There
should be a 1/100 change of dying of botulism poisoning after eating a
self-made tin. --ijon

[10]: On occasion, a random event might occur. The dungeon might flood,
or a freak storm might start. There might be a gas leak, or maybe a
volcano erupts. Who knows? --TheShrewdDude

[11]: The current dungeons are so terribly boring. Why not have
-random- levels where there might be a sea (as opposed to checkerboard
pools), a chasm full of lava, a storm cloud, or an ice area?
--TheShrewdDude

[12]: There should also be areas that are date-related. For example,
one might expect a snow area in wintertime, and a tree grove in spring.
--TheShrewdDude

[13]: Credit to n54 and Xarann: New conduct: The Counter-Pacifist - You
must cause conflict throughout the whole game. --TheShrewdDude

[14]: miser conduct: you may not use gold or interact with shopkeepers
in any way (except as a projectile) --teabing

[15]: Gold golems, or any golem, should eat their constituent parts.
When doing so, they heal fully and gain 50% more hitpoints, as with the
endgame Riders' effects. --TheShrewdDude

[16]: When wizards die, Death should visit them. (think diskworld)
--Botje

[17]: Critical hit: Certain monsters and weapons can have special
critical hit abilities. You might lose an arm and be unable to wear a
shield or twoweapon, get your head bashed in and suffer a concussion,
or get paralyzed from a blow to the spine. Of course, there should be
magical and conventional remedies for these maladies, so that it isn't
game-wrecking when you become a... --TheShrewdDude

[18]: The Riders should be able to summon nasties, specifically angels
and demons. --Thvor


Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
